  "body": "Found while the cut gate of v0.21.0 was red (run 43739171721, step `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`).\n\nWhat happens:\n- A whole-model 3D Pocket with the Adaptive strategy and no area control clears the stock around the part out to the stock outline (#1774, PR #1780).\n- On the 60 mm bore part in 70 x 70 stock, each level is then a wide ring with the part as its island.\n- The HSM plan exceeds its budgets on that ring: about 600.4k outline vertices against the limit 600k (605.2k on Windows), and 124740 moves against the limit 120000.\n- Offset rings cut four of the five levels. The notes name each level. The path verifies clean. There is no gouge.\n\nExpected: the Adaptive strategy plans the stock ring within its budgets, or the budgets fit that region.\n\nWorkaround: set Tool containment to Inside on the operation. Then the pocket plans only the bore and Adaptive cuts each level.\n\nEvidence: `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. The cut repaired the test with Tool containment Inside (commit `bf752be65` on `release/v0.21.0`), thus the default case has no test now.\n\nDone means: the default whole-model Adaptive 3D Pocket on that fixture cuts each level with the Adaptive plan, with no budget note, and a test pins it.\n",
